# Import probe, unit dl-a

Tree: the pre-ship worktree at the issue-tree commit (see the brief's Pre-ship record); olean tree filldl-oleans; each probe checked alone with scripts/lean_check_tree.sh (PATH with ~/.elan/bin, TCSLIB_OLEANS set).
A probe file is `#check @Name` per line inside `namespace TCSlib.Cryptography.Candidates` with the owned file's `open`s; a Lean error on a line marks that name UNRESOLVED.

Worktree HEAD: 5f2771631fe853dae9c2aa44791ae5b0e09c95eb
## Classification
- Present in the owned files' scope: every name of the seven dl-a sketches and every name of the draft's text other than those listed next.
- Unresolved, expected: the 14 dl-b and dl-c targets and ddhReal/ddhRandom (downstream files); ddhExpo, egUnit, egGenParts, egEncParts (named in
  statClose_sampleBelowL's docstring as its consumers in ElGamal; not needed by dl-a).
- Present but not imported by any owned file (templates, read as models; not authorized as imports): TCSlib.Cryptography.statClose_permFromCoins
  (Asymptotic/Permutations), TCSlib.Cryptography.polyTimeComputable_prgPadFun (Asymptotic/Encryption),
  TCSlib.Cryptography.MultiMsg.polyTimeComputable_preFun/_postFun/_blockMapFun (Asymptotic/MultiMessageLemmas; the draft's bare names do not
  resolve outside namespace MultiMsg). Adding any of these imports would create no cycle (cyclecheck.py), but none is needed.
- Imports dl-a must be authorized: none.


